{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00370",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.73,
      "end_seconds": 8.12,
      "duration_seconds": 7.39,
      "text": "Doctor, the patient's with us now. I did the usual checks at the front, so just say when you want them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 12.91,
      "end_seconds": 16.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Great. Hello, come in and sit down. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.65,
      "end_seconds": 25.29,
      "duration_seconds": 7.64,
      "text": "So, I've been passing out once last week, doctor. I took the morning off to come in today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.49,
      "end_seconds": 28.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "And when did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.58,
      "end_seconds": 36.37,
      "duration_seconds": 7.79,
      "text": "Oh, it's been about two weeks, I'm fairly sure. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.69,
      "end_seconds": 50.36,
      "duration_seconds": 9.67,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse. It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.84,
      "end_seconds": 60.61,
      "duration_seconds": 8.77,
      "text": "A six out of ten, I suppose. It settles a little with lying down. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.42,
      "end_seconds": 63.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Does it come along with anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.1,
      "end_seconds": 74.45,
      "duration_seconds": 9.35,
      "text": "A bit of lightheadedness since then goes along with it, most of the time. The bit of lightheadedness since then? That's been since last Tuesday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.9,
      "end_seconds": 76.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "How much is it bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.48,
      "end_seconds": 78.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "It's moderate, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.56,
      "end_seconds": 82.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "One moment, the system's being slow today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.92,
      "end_seconds": 83.66,
      "duration_seconds": 0.74,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.89,
      "end_seconds": 103.45,
      "duration_seconds": 7.56,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Let me check a few things. Any tongue biting, shaking or jerking or confusion afterwards?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.23,
      "end_seconds": 106.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "No, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.62,
      "end_seconds": 109.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "What about loss of bladder control?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.38,
      "end_seconds": 115.42,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "So, uh, no, I haven't had any loss of bladder control."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.27,
      "end_seconds": 129.94,
      "duration_seconds": 13.67,
      "text": "It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.83,
      "end_seconds": 132.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "That's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 132.8,
      "end_seconds": 137.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Pressure 117 over 69, pulse 79."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.44,
      "end_seconds": 138.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.59,
      "end_seconds": 143.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just scrolling back through your chart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.77,
      "end_seconds": 144.57,
      "duration_seconds": 0.8,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.41,
      "end_seconds": 156.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Any long-term health problems I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.53,
      "end_seconds": 166.73,
      "duration_seconds": 7.2,
      "text": "I mean, uh, yes, high blood pressure. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.98,
      "end_seconds": 170.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.15,
      "end_seconds": 172.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "It's perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.7,
      "end_seconds": 177.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.19,
      "end_seconds": 183.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Yes, latex, it gives me a rash on my hands."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.07,
      "end_seconds": 187.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just typing this up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.52,
      "end_seconds": 206.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "That's saved, thanks for waiting. Have you had any surgery before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.7,
      "end_seconds": 209.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Just my gallbladder removed, in 2016."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.66,
      "end_seconds": 212.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "What medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.61,
      "end_seconds": 221.97,
      "duration_seconds": 8.36,
      "text": "Right, I take ramipril, 5 milligrams, every morning for my blood pressure. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.55,
      "end_seconds": 226.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "Can I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.83,
      "end_seconds": 227.53,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.72,
      "end_seconds": 230.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Let me check your reflexes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.32,
      "end_seconds": 242.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "No murmurs on listening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.75,
      "end_seconds": 245.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Just relax, I'll be quick."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.05,
      "end_seconds": 260.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "Your pulse is regular and there's a small bruise on the right side of the head."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.43,
      "end_seconds": 289.6,
      "duration_seconds": 25.17,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. Good, that's all I need to examine. Let me gather my thoughts and then we'll talk it through together. Putting it all together, this looks most like a simple faint, probably reflex-related. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've been passing out once last week for about two weeks, and no confusion afterwards or shaking or jerking."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 290.41,
      "end_seconds": 293.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Oh, exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.15,
      "end_seconds": 310.22,
      "duration_seconds": 16.07,
      "text": "Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 311.52,
      "end_seconds": 313.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.9,
      "end_seconds": 335.68,
      "duration_seconds": 21.78,
      "text": "I'm going to order a Holter monitor, for syncope. Let's get blood tests, for syncope. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. Drink enough water and avoid standing still for long stretches, and sit if you feel it coming. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.13,
      "end_seconds": 344.54,
      "duration_seconds": 7.41,
      "text": "I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if you pass out again, especially with chest pain or palpitations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 345.51,
      "end_seconds": 346.21,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.65,
      "end_seconds": 355.48,
      "duration_seconds": 7.83,
      "text": "Please come and see me in two weeks. Can you run through the plan with me quickly, just to be certain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 356.97,
      "end_seconds": 360.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "So, I come back in two weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.32,
      "end_seconds": 365.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Good. Look after yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 366.55,
      "end_seconds": 369.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Thank you. I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
}